cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this repository, please cite it as below."
title: "ai-energy-claim-provenance: recomputation and provenance for the self-calculated figures in 'O Brasil virou destino de data center e não mede o que eles gastam'"
abstract: >-
  Companion repository for an article that traced each widely circulated figure
  about the energy use of artificial intelligence back to its primary source.
  It holds the five sets of numbers the article calculates itself - the
  122-language energy divide measured by Deng et al., the series of five PJM
  capacity auctions, the variation of the US residential electricity price, the
  sum of Microsoft's per-location datacenter electricity against its regional
  total, and the count of NVIDIA submissions to the power category of MLPerf
  Inference: Datacenter. Every published number exists here as a test
  assertion; a single SHA-256 chain seals code, frozen evidence and derived
  results; and a second track re-derives every frozen figure by downloading the
  primary documents from their publishers.
